Subject: [PATCH] Add passwordless share link for the Helfer view
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New "An Helfer teilen" button in the Admin toolbar (web only) opens a
modal with a direct link to the current event's read-only Helfer view
— no login, no token/password, since the Helfer view was already
login-free and read-only. The link is just the app's current URL with
?event=<id> appended (src/shared/data/shareLink.ts), so it works
unmodified under any deploy base path (e.g. GitHub Pages' /schichtplan/).

App.tsx reads that query param once at load (getSharedEventId()),
forces Helfer mode, and passes the event id down so HelferScreen
pre-selects it instead of defaulting to the first event.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Qm1ZJgsnaADwCEstGj8Dvj
